<Item XName="Note1" UserName="Note1" Type="Notes">
<Selected><T>Bool</T><D>0</D></Selected>
<Text>&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt; &#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoTitle style=&quot;BORDER-TOP: medium none; BORDER-RIGHT: medium none; BORDER-BOTTOM: windowtext 0.75pt solid; PADDING-BOTTOM: 1pt; PADDING-TOP: 0in; PADDING-LEFT: 0in; BORDER-LEFT: medium none; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt; PADDING-RIGHT: 0in&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;STRONG&gt;&lt;FONT size=6 face=Arial&gt;PhaseArray_Radar&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/STRONG&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; FONT-FAMILY: Arial; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;Keysight Technologies SystemVue Template Workspace&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;?xml:namespace prefix = &quot;o&quot; ns = &quot;urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office&quot; /&gt;&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P class=MsoNormal style=&quot;TEXT-ALIGN: center; MARGIN: 0in 0in 0pt&quot; align=center&gt;&lt;SPAN style=&quot;FONT-SIZE: 10pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;FONT size=4&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/SPAN&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;This workspace demonstrates how to use SystemVue and SystemVue Engine to analysis phase array&amp;nbsp;pattern MATLAB and have that signal available back in MATLAB to do further processing.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;Make sure you add the folder &amp;lt;SystemVue Installation Dir&amp;gt;\Baseband_Link to your MATLAB search path.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5&gt;Copy this workspace and the MATLAB scripts (PhaseArray_Radar.m) located in the same folder as this workspace to a directory where you have write access to.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot;&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;P&gt;&lt;FONT size=6&gt;Exercises/Experiments for design &lt;EM&gt;PhaseArray_Radar&lt;/EM&gt;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/P&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;OL&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Open the script PhaseArray_Radar.m in MATLAB and read the code and&amp;nbsp;comments to understand the flow.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;Run the script. The first time you run the script, SystemVue Engine starts and there is some&amp;nbsp;one-time initialization delay. Next time you run the script it should run faster.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;In the matlab, the simulation process is 1. Specify parameters -&amp;gt;2.Run the &lt;EM&gt;Radar_PhaseArray&lt;/EM&gt; analysis and generate the pattern data-&amp;gt;3. Collect the pattern data in matlab and plot the pattern in matlab enviroment.&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&#x000D;&#x000A;&lt;LI&gt;&lt;FONT size=5 face=Arial&gt;In matlab enviroment, coustumer could specify the array configration, array amplitude error, phase shift error, and position errors, and then&amp;nbsp;observe these errors affact the pattern main lobe and side lobe.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/FONT&gt;&lt;/LI&gt;&lt;/OL&gt;</Text>
